=== REASONING ===
The boundary is additive: Store remains the in-memory L1 and RedisSignalCache remains optional L2. The new hybrid implementation updates Store first, mirrors to Redis only in hybrid mode when Redis exists, and returns Redis errors after the L1 update so callers can surface degradation without losing local state.

Distributed reads prefer timestamp-aware Redis values in hybrid mode and only return values that satisfy the existing freshness threshold. Local read preference and local runtime mode always read Store, preserving the telemetry/FSM/session hot path and the LIVE_SIGNAL_STORE_MODE=local rollback contract.

Warmup is limited to Redis-to-L1 hydration and does not import repository or persistence packages into internal\signal. Durable signal_log writes and reads remain owned elsewhere.

